ntrip is the RTK correction client. It is skipped for now because:

- it needs mavros_msgs, which is neither in the workspace nor installed by
  rosdep, so the package fails to configure;
- the caster it is configured against (UWA_Campus at 3.143.243.81:2101) is
  unreachable, so it cannot be tested even if it built.

RTK is not on the critical path: Autoware localises with NDT against a point
cloud map, and GNSS only supplies the initial pose - pose_initializer accepts
a 5 m error. Delete this file and install ros-humble-mavros-msgs once the
correction source is sorted out.
